        "title": "Disambiguate duplicate session titles",
        "body": "Closes #954.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Sessions page rendered raw gateway display names, so forked or otherwise colliding sessions could be indistinguishable.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Reuse one session-title formatter across native chat and the Sessions page.\n- Add deterministic numeric suffixes when key-derived qualifiers still collide, without exposing raw session keys.\n- Preserve the original session keys for navigation and actions.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `dotnet test ./tests/OpenClaw.Tray.Tests/OpenClaw.Tray.Tests.csproj --no-restore --filter 'FullyQualifiedName~SessionTitleFormatterTests|FullyQualifiedName~OpenClawChatDataProviderTests'`: 234 passed.\n- `dotnet build ./tests/OpenClaw.Tray.Tests/OpenClaw.Tray.Tests.csproj -c Debug -r win-x64 --no-restore`: 0 warnings, 0 errors.\n- GitHub Actions Windows matrix: 8 passed, 4 expected skips, 0 failures, including the full test job, three E2E shards, and win-x64/win-arm64 builds.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nCurrent-head regression tests map equal `OpenClaw Windows Tray` display names to distinct visible titles while retaining their original routing keys. Coverage also proves multi-segment and legacy-key collisions remain distinct and stable across channel filtering.\n\nWindows Sessions-page screenshot or UIA output: Not verified / blocked on this macOS host.",
